From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:13:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: link libcec and libdvdnav into kodi

libcec is built static with the Linux kernel CEC framework, which it
leaves off by default, so it reaches /dev/cec0, and without X11 RandR,
which a GBM build has no use for.

libdvdnav, with libdvdread and libdvdcss, is linked in rather than
wrapped into a shared library loaded at runtime: the navigator calls
it directly, and DllDvdNav goes. Windows, which ships its own DLL, is
left out.
---
 cmake/modules/FindCEC.cmake                   |   8 +-
 cmake/modules/FindLibDvd.cmake                |   5 +-
 tools/depends/target/cec/CEC-VERSION          |   2 +-
 xbmc/DllPaths_generated.h.in                  |   1 -
 .../DVDInputStreams/CMakeLists.txt            |   1 -
 .../DVDInputStreamNavigator.cpp               | 210 ++++++------
 .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamNavigator.h |   3 +-
 .../VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DllDvdNav.h   | 303 ------------------
 8 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 423 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/DllDvdNav.h

